      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The race realism movement argues that inherent biological differences exist between racial groups, which they claim directly correlate with differences in cognitive abilities and IQ. Proponents often cite genetic studies, though these are frequently misinterpreted, to support the idea that certain traits are genetically fixed within specific populations. They maintain that environmental factors alone cannot account for the observed disparities in intelligence across different racial groups. Essentially, their core belief is that race is a meaningful biological category that dictates intellectual capacity.",
